{:edb/db-before-t 2699 :edb/db-after-t 2700 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536012 50 #inst "2026-10-15T18:34:44.213Z" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186115242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557414 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186115242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557415 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186115242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557416 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186115242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557419 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186115242 1038 #edb/ref 17592186557444 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186115242 1040 #edb/ref 17592186557445 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557410 1080 "k=-4" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557410 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557410 1083 #uuid "040900c0-cbe2-5a3b-bf63-00c6502b1713" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557411 1080 "k=0" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557411 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557411 1083 #uuid "124ff963-b72f-5e65-b019-142dc4093408" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557412 1080 "k=-6" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557412 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557412 1083 #uuid "27dd0a80-4647-5fb3-bf6e-d022bfd8b7be" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557413 1080 "k=-2" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557413 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557413 1083 #uuid "2ce26fa4-9b16-5f35-94ea-df9965919477" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557414 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557436 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557414 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557414 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-5 \\\\ 2x+ky &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557414 1072 #uuid "2d5b5966-d0b2-51ba-a7a1-c76ebe8e6658" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557414 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & k & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-5 \\\\ (k-6)y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557415 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557422 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557415 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557415 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ -2x+ky &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557415 1072 #uuid "364e838c-b667-5333-9687-aeee90961e0c" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557415 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-3,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557416 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557435 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557416 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557416 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ 3x+ky &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557416 1072 #uuid "4508cab0-6e88-59d6-a9c3-7b9fc61a9c9d" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557416 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & k & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & k+6 & -12\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=5 \\\\ (k+6)y &=-12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-6,$ then the second equation is $0=-12,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-6.$" 13194139536012 17592186045443 true] [17592186557417 1080 "k=3" 13194139536012 17592186045443